+        // THE INDENT A LINE WROTE AS SPACES IS AN INDENT, NOT TEXT.
+        //
+        // A page that aligns a column by drawing spaces - an R console's column headings, a
+        // shell transcript's continuation - arrives here as a run whose text begins with n
+        // ASCII spaces, and b.x is the LEFT EDGE OF THE FIRST SPACE. The indent is therefore
+        // never written as w:ind: it is n x the space advance of whichever face ends up
+        // rendering the line. With the face the page used the ink lands where the page put it
+        // and nothing is wrong. With a substitute it moves by n x the change in advance, and n
+        // is not small: 392_statistical_console_output's "Estimate Std. Error" row is 20 spaces,
+        // 79.5 pt of ink offset in DejaVu Sans Mono and 36.2 pt when the same spaces are set in
+        // Liberation Sans (measured: the ink lands at 64.2 instead of 107.5).
+        //
+        // So the spaces come out of the run text and what they stood for becomes a real
+        // w:ind w:left: the ink is pinned at b.inkX - the x the page drew the first glyph that
