+        // - and the line stops depending on any face's space advance. Where the rendering face
+        // is the page's own the two numbers are the same, so the change is position-neutral
+        // there and only bites under substitution. Left-aligned only: a centred or right line
+        // has its left edge delegated to the renderer already, and its indent is not this.
+        int leadTw = 0;
+        int leadSp = 0;
